# Governs the lab/assessment image build. The compose files build with
# `context: .` (this directory) and `dockerfile: lab/Dockerfile`, so THIS file,
# not lab/.dockerignore, decides what the builder receives.
#
# RULE (production launch failure 2026-10-22, tag v0.0.2): the DLI launch
# tarball is cut from task1/ and this file is honoured there as well as in the
# image build. Everything the VM needs at launch (docker-compose*.yml, .env,
# nginx.conf, data_sources, load-course-data.py, deploy/, dind/, .launchignore)
# must therefore NOT be listed here, even though the image never copies it:
# lab/Dockerfile copies specific paths only, so an unlisted file costs nothing.
# .launchignore alone decides what stays out of the tarball.

# Secrets and local config. .env-dev holds the dev NGC key: never in an image
# and never on a learner VM (.launchignore lists it too).
.env-dev

# Host-side tooling. task1/tests is the offline gate and task1/scripts the
# publishing helpers; neither is image content or launch content. The grader's
# tests ship with its code.
tests
scripts

# Learner output on a devbox (bind-mounted tree); never image content. That
# includes what the coding agent writes under work/agent/.
lab/task/work
# No git repository is ever baked into an image, wherever a devbox left one.
**/.git

# Caches, data, checkpoints.
.git
**/data
**/models
**/results
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.Trash*
**/*.zip
**/*.tgz
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tar
**/devonly*
**/skill_walkthrough
